# 1. What is defined as "Identity" in this ecosystem?

For your demo, I would define identity as:

> **Identity is the cryptographically verifiable representation of an entity, workload, agent, or delegation context that allows a system to determine who or what is making a request, on whose behalf, and with what authority.**

In an AI-agent ecosystem, there are actually several identities:

```text
Human Identity
      │
      ▼
Application / Session Identity
      │
      ▼
Parent Agent Identity
      │
      ▼
Child Agent Identity
      │
      ▼
Tool / MCP Identity
      │
      ▼
Workload / Sandbox Identity
```

And these should not be collapsed into one `user_id`.

For example:

```text
Akhil
  │
  │ authorized
  ▼
Marketing Agent
  │
  │ delegates
  ▼
Identity Resolution Agent
  │
  │ calls
  ▼
Customer Data MCP
  │
  │ accesses
  ▼
CDP Identity Graph
```

The system needs to preserve the entire relationship.

A useful identity object therefore becomes:

```text
WHO
 └── agent-123

ON_BEHALF_OF
 └── marketing-user-456

PARENT
 └── campaign-agent-001

PURPOSE
 └── credit-card-customer-acquisition

CAPABILITY
 └── identity.resolve

RESOURCE
 └── CDP.identity.graph

CONSTRAINT
 └── campaign_id = 789

EXPIRY
 └── 5 minutes

PROVENANCE
 └── signed delegation chain
```

That is much richer than traditional:

```text
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

