# 11. Identity-governance pitfalls in CDP

You can demonstrate these five.

### Pitfall 1 — Over-broad identity resolution

```text
Agent:
"Resolve customer."

Actual access:
CRM + transaction + behavioral + household + financial data
```

The task only required:

```text
CRM + behavioral
```

But the agent receives more.

---

### Pitfall 2 — Delegation privilege explosion

```text
Campaign Agent
      ↓
Identity Agent
      ↓
Audience Agent
      ↓
Activation Agent
```

If every agent inherits the original user's privileges:

```text
Privilege = UNION(all parent privileges)
```

you eventually get:

```text
Agent 4 = enormous privilege set
```

Your governance model should instead perform:

```text
Privilege(child)
    =
Privilege(parent)
    ∩
Required capability
    ∩
Purpose
    ∩
Resource scope
    ∩
Policy
```

That's **least agency**, not merely least privilege.

---

### Pitfall 3 — Identity collision

Imagine:

```text
John Smith
john.smith@gmail.com
device-123
CRM-789
```

The model concludes:

```text
all = same person
```

But the confidence is only:

```text
0.61
```

Your EdgeMind-style governance layer could say:

```text
confidence < 0.70
        │
        ▼
Do NOT activate audience
        │
        ▼
Human review
```

This gives your confidence-gated architecture a concrete enterprise use case.

---

### Pitfall 4 — Purpose drift

The agent was authorized for:

```text
purpose =
"credit-card acquisition"
```

but starts querying:

```text
loan history
```

because the model believes it will improve targeting.

Technically:

```text
ACCESS = ALLOWED
```

Governance:

```text
PURPOSE = NOT ALLOWED
```

Therefore:

```text
DENY
```

This is one of the strongest arguments for your architecture.

---

### Pitfall 5 — Provenance loss

Without governance:

```text
User
 ↓
Campaign Agent
 ↓
Identity Agent
 ↓
Audience Agent
 ↓
MCP
```

Six hours later someone asks:

> "Why was customer X added to this audience?"

You need:

```text
WHO
WHAT
WHY
ON WHOSE BEHALF
WHICH AGENT
WHICH MODEL
WHICH DATA
WHICH POLICY
WHICH DELEGATION
WHICH CONFIDENCE
WHEN
```

That's your **agent provenance graph**.

