# 12. Governance in MCP as policy

I would introduce a policy object before every MCP invocation.

For example:

```yaml
agent:
  id: identity-agent-01

delegation:
  parent: campaign-agent-01
  root_subject: user-123
  purpose: credit-card-acquisition

capabilities:
  - identity.resolve

resources:
  - cdp.customer.identity

constraints:
  max_records: 1000
  pii: masked
  transaction_data: denied

confidence:
  minimum: 0.80

expires_in: 300
```

Then:

```text
Agent
  │
  │ MCP call
  ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│ Identity Governance     │
│                         │
│ Who?                    │
│ Parent?                 │
│ Purpose?                │
│ Capability?             │
│ Resource?               │
│ Confidence?             │
│ Expiry?                 │
│ Delegation valid?       │
└───────────┬─────────────┘
